# The door (S-0066/D-1): an attempt reads the skills its profile declared and
# no others. mimo 0.1.15 loads skills from `.mimocode` — where equipment is
# copied (S-0063/D-19), so that root stays open — and from the open-standard
# `.agents`; `.claude`, `.codex` and `.opencode` load only when their
# `MIMOCODE_ENABLE_*_SKILLS` switch is set, and nothing here sets one. This
# repository's worktree carries skills under `.agents` and `.claude`, none
# pinned or hashed, so the regime digest would claim more than it knows.
#
# Sourced by `run` and by the build's door probe, which lists the skills a
# built image loads with these values and fails if a closed root shows up.
MIMOCODE_DISABLE_AGENTS_SKILLS=1
# `.claude`'s agents, commands, MCP servers and CLAUDE.md prompt, which mimo
# reads for Claude Code compatibility whether or not its skills are enabled.
MIMOCODE_DISABLE_CLAUDE_CODE=1
